        "title": "Introduction",
        "key_prerequisites": [],
        "has_content_in_snapshot": true,
        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>How can we calculate the integral of a sum of functions, like <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\displaystyle \\int (x+x^3)\\,\\textrm d x?]</span> </p>",
            "readable_text": "How can we calculate the integral of a sum of functions, like [MATH: \\displaystyle \\int (x+x^3)\\,\\textrm d x?]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>According to the <strong>sum rule</strong>, the integral of the sum of functions is equal to the sum of the integrals of each function:</p>",
            "readable_text": "According to the sum rule, the integral of the sum of functions is equal to the sum of the integrals of each function:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\int (f(x) \\pm g(x))\\,\\textrm d x = \\int f(x) \\,\\textrm d x \\pm \\int g(x) \\,\\textrm d x.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: \\int (f(x) \\pm g(x))\\,\\textrm d x = \\int f(x) \\,\\textrm d x \\pm \\int g(x) \\,\\textrm d x.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>In our case, we have\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: \u222b(x + x^{3})dx|= \u222bxdx + \u222bx^{3}dx; = ((x^{2})/(2) + c_{1}) + ((x^{4})/(4) + c_{2}); = (1)/(2)x^{2} + (1)/(4)x^{4} + (c_{1} + c_{2}); = (1)/(2)x^{2} + (1)/(4)x^{4} + C,]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "In our case, we have\n[MATH: \u222b(x + x^{3})dx|= \u222bxdx + \u222bx^{3}dx; = ((x^{2})/(2) + c_{1}) + ((x^{4})/(4) + c_{2}); = (1)/(2)x^{2} + (1)/(4)x^{4} + (c_{1} + c_{2}); = (1)/(2)x^{2} + (1)/(4)x^{4} + C,]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>where we renamed <span class=\"math\">[MATH: c_1+c_2=C.]</span> (The sum of two arbitrary constants is itself an arbitrary constant.)</p>",
            "readable_text": "where we renamed [MATH: c_1+c_2=C.] (The sum of two arbitrary constants is itself an arbitrary constant.)",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Content:\nHow can we calculate the integral of a sum of functions, like [MATH: \\displaystyle \\int (x+x^3)\\,\\textrm d x?]\n\nContent:\nAccording to the sum rule, the integral of the sum of functions is equal to the sum of the integrals of each function:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \\int (f(x) \\pm g(x))\\,\\textrm d x = \\int f(x) \\,\\textrm d x \\pm \\int g(x) \\,\\textrm d x.]\n\nContent:\nIn our case, we have\n[MATH: \u222b(x + x^{3})dx|= \u222bxdx + \u222bx^{3}dx; = ((x^{2})/(2) + c_{1}) + ((x^{4})/(4) + c_{2}); = (1)/(2)x^{2} + (1)/(4)x^{4} + (c_{1} + c_{2}); = (1)/(2)x^{2} + (1)/(4)x^{4} + C,]\n\nContent:\nwhere we renamed [MATH: c_1+c_2=C.] (The sum of two arbitrary constants is itself an arbitrary constant.)"
      },
