    "readable_text": "Item 1 \u2014 Tutorial: Introduction\n\nContent:\nHow can we calculate the integral of a sum of functions, like [MATH: \\displaystyle \\int (x+x^3)\\,\\textrm d x?]\n\nContent:\nAccording to the sum rule, the integral of the sum of functions is equal to the sum of the integrals of each function:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \\int (f(x) \\pm g(x))\\,\\textrm d x = \\int f(x) \\,\\textrm d x \\pm \\int g(x) \\,\\textrm d x.]\n\nContent:\nIn our case, we have\n[MATH: \u222b(x + x^{3})dx|= \u222bxdx + \u222bx^{3}dx; = ((x^{2})/(2) + c_{1}) + ((x^{4})/(4) + c_{2}); = (1)/(2)x^{2} + (1)/(4)x^{4} + (c_{1} + c_{2}); = (1)/(2)x^{2} + (1)/(4)x^{4} + C,]\n\nContent:\nwhere we renamed [MATH: c_1+c_2=C.] (The sum of two arbitrary constants is itself an arbitrary constant.)\n\n---\n\nItem 2 \u2014 Example: Computing an Integral Using the Sum Rule\n\nExample Prompt:\nFind the integral of [MATH: x^2 + 1.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nApplying the sum rule, we compute the sum of the integrals of each function:\n\n[MATH: \u222bx^{2} + 1dx|= \u222bx^{2}dx + \u222b1dx; = \u222bx^{2}dx + \u222bx^{0}dx; = ((x^{2 + 1})/(2 + 1)) + x + C; = (1)/(3)x^{3} + x + C]\n\n---\n\nItem 3 \u2014 Question 1\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: \u222bsqrt(x) \u2212 3dx =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: (3root(x^{2}, 3))/(2) \u2212 3x]\nb. [MATH: (sqrt(x^{3}))/(3) \u2212 3x + C]\nc. [MATH: (3xsqrt(x^{3}))/(2) \u2212 3x + C]\nd. [MATH: (2xroot(x, 3))/(3) + 3 + C]\ne. [MATH: (2sqrt(x^{3}))/(3) \u2212 3x + C]\n\n---\n\nItem 4 \u2014 Question 2\n\nPrompt:\nFind the antiderivative of [MATH: sqrt(x^{5}) + (1)/(sqrt(x^{5})).]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: (4sqrt(x^{5}))/(7) \u2212 (7)/(5sqrt(x^{3})) + C]\nb. [MATH: (2sqrt(x^{7}))/(7) \u2212 (2)/(3sqrt(x^{3})) + C]\nc. [MATH: (2sqrt(x^{3}))/(7) + (2)/(3sqrt(x^{5})) + C]\nd. [MATH: (2sqrt(x^{7}))/(3) + (5)/(3sqrt(x^{3})) + C]\ne. [MATH: (3sqrt(x^{3}))/(7) \u2212 (11)/(3sqrt(x^{7})) + C]\n\n---\n\nItem 5 \u2014 Tutorial: Combining the Constant Factor and Sum Rules\n\nContent:\nFor more complicated functions consisting of the sum of functions multiplied by constants, we can combine the constant factor and sum rules as follows:\n[MATH: \\int k_1 f(x) \\pm k_2 g(x)\\,\\textrm d x = k_1\\int f(x) \\,\\textrm d x \\pm k_2\\int g(x) \\,\\textrm d x]\n\n---\n\nItem 6 \u2014 Example: Computing an Integral Using the Sum and Constant Factor Rules\n\nExample Prompt:\nCalculate [MATH: \\displaystyle \\int 2 x^3 - x \\,\\textrm d x.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nUsing the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n[MATH: \u222b2x^{3} \u2212 xdx|= 2\u222bx^{3}dx \u2212 \u222bxdx; = 2((x^{3 + 1})/(3 + 1)) \u2212 ((x^{1 + 1})/(1 + 1)) + C; = 2((x^{4})/(4)) \u2212 ((x^{2})/(2)) + C; = (x^{4})/(2) \u2212 (x^{2})/(2) + C.]\n\n---\n\nItem 7 \u2014 Question 3\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: \u222b12x^{3} + 5xdx =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 12x^{2} + (5x^{2})/(2) + C]\nb. [MATH: 3x^{2} + (5x^{2})/(2) + C]\nc. [MATH: 3x^{4} + (5x^{2})/(2) + C]\nd. [MATH: 3x^{4} + (5x^{3})/(2) + C]\ne. [MATH: 6x^{4} + (5x^{4})/(2) + C]\n\n---\n\nItem 8 \u2014 Question 4\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: \u222b(1)/(x^{2}) \u2212 3xdx =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: \u2212 (2x^{2})/(3) \u2212 (1)/(x) + C]\nb. [MATH: (3x^{2})/(2) \u2212 (1)/(x) + C]\nc. [MATH: \u2212 (3x)/(2) \u2212 (1)/(x^{2}) + C]\nd. [MATH: \u2212 (3x^{2})/(2) \u2212 (1)/(x) + C]\ne. [MATH: \u2212 (3x)/(2) + (1)/(x) + C]\n\n---\n\nItem 9 \u2014 Example: Integrating Sums of Power Functions\n\nExample Prompt:\nCalculate [MATH: \\displaystyle \\int \\left( 5(\\sqrt{x})^{3} - 4 x^2 + 5\\right) \\,\\textrm d x.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nUsing the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n[MATH: \u222b(5(sqrt(x))^{3} \u2212 4x^{2} + 5)dx|= \u222b(5x^{3/2} \u2212 4x^{2} + 5)dx; = 5\u222bx^{3/2}dx \u2212 4\u222bx^{2}dx + 5\u222b1dx; = 5((x^{5/2})/((5)/(2))) \u2212 4((x^{3})/(3)) + 5(x) + C; = 5 \u22c5 (2)/(5)x^{5/2} \u2212 (4)/(3)x^{3} + 5x + C; = 2sqrt(x^{5}) \u2212 (4)/(3)x^{3} + 5x + C.]\n\n---\n\nItem 10 \u2014 Question 5\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: \u222b(x^{2} \u2212 sqrt(x) + 2)dx =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: (x^{3} \u2212 3sqrt(x^{3}) + 6x)/(3) + C]\nb. [MATH: (x^{3} \u2212 2sqrt(x^{3}) + 6x)/(3) + C]\nc. [MATH: (x^{3} + 2root(x^{2}, 3) + 2x)/(3) + C]\nd. [MATH: (x^{3} + 3sqrt(x^{3}) + 6x)/(3) + C]\ne. [MATH: (x^{3} \u2212 2sqrt(x^{3}) + 2x)/(3) + C]\n\n---\n\nItem 11 \u2014 Question 6\n\nPrompt:\nFind the antiderivative of\n[MATH: 4x^{7} + root(x, 5) \u2212 (1)/(root(x^{13}, 7)).]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: (x^{8})/(2) \u2212 (5root(x^{6}, 5))/(3) + (7)/(6root(x^{6}, 7)) + C]\nb. [MATH: (x^{8})/(2) + (6root(x^{6}, 5))/(5) + (7)/(6root(x^{6}, 7)) + C]\nc. [MATH: (x^{8})/(8) + (5root(x^{6}, 5))/(6) + (7)/(6root(x^{6}, 7)) + C]\nd. [MATH: (x^{8})/(2) + (5root(x^{6}, 5))/(6) + (7)/(6root(x^{6}, 7)) + C]\ne. [MATH: (x^{8})/(4) + (5root(x^{5}, 6))/(6) + (7)/(6root(x^{6}, 7)) + C]"
  }
